  openingDialogue:
  - 'In this level, the beams have a <b>thinner profile</b>! To compensate, <b>the
    mass of the weight has been reduced</b>. '
  - Keep in mind that the <b>compressed members will break more easily due to the
    thin profile</b>.
  - "This is a result of the width of the cross-section being raised to the fourth
    power when calculating <b>Euler\u2019s Critical Load</b>."
  - To prevent your compressed members from buckling, make sure they are <b>not too
    long</b>!
  - Make sure to select the right material in your <b>toolbox</b> on the bottom of
    your screen.
  - This is the final level, so please save my few remaining braincells.
